      "observations": [
        "Full four-file owned production/new182line browser test/manifest/fake-server diff read. Historical policy no longer accepts merely because the URI lacks nsIMsgMessageUrl. It gets canonical message URI or raw spec, looks up the database header, accepts non-mailbox unknown messages and otherwise applies remote-content policy. Historical mailbox remains special so file-backed messages without a DB header still reach the lower policy, whose null-header path rejects. This is not a statement that every URI with a DB entry bypasses earlier policy checks.",
        "Accepted code uses a later GetPotentialMsgHdr helper and returns accept when it has no header; the owned explicit mailbox exception is no longer in that selected current branch. Keep that later structure separate from the historical guard, rather than claiming identical unknown/file-backed behavior. Current helper delegates to actual message-service MessageURIToMsgHdr; other permission, compose, remote-page and header exceptions remain separate scopes.",
        "The new test creates a loopback EWS account/login and HTTP image endpoint, syncs one HTML message, waits for folder change and selected message load, then directly asserts warning/remoteContent notification and !imageRequested. The HTTP handler records an attempted request before404/opaque-response handling, so this test does not need successful rendering to detect a request. All4 added assertions have nonempty should messages. The copied signed-body comment is inaccurate for this generated unsigned HTML message; no OpenPGP signature is established.",
        "Initial cleanup stops EWS/closes connections but leaves account/logins; follow-up3300 owns their removal. Current cleanup uses async removeAllLoginsAsync after account removal and is still registered after account/login setup. No speculative complete cleanup claim follows; this study writes no test or try/finally. Fake EWS constructor moves version default into destructuring, which changes explicit-null handling compared with ??; defaults only apply to undefined. No default value/type equivalence is assumed for null.",
        "No browser/server, external image request, privacy/security experiment, test, build, lint, runtime or accessibility validation ran. Static assertions are coverage evidence, not proof every protocol/URL/permission combination is safe.",
        "Reuse exact complete primary Bug1910983 already read for3300, retaining its explicit correction from remote media not loading to media shown by default and needing blocking. Read full D258726 timeline/all1actual inline, no summary edits. Author initially withdraws premature review to investigate tests, receives advice about existing content-policy tests/mochitest server, then supplies EWS-specific test and requests review. Reviewer reports works nicely and accepts; no fresh test result is inferred.",
        "The inline describes moving the fake-server version default for argument consistency, but exact source analysis retains the explicit-null behavior difference between destructuring default and ?? instead of treating every value as equivalent. Own test probe observes attempted requests before404; message DB criterion, historical mailbox exception and later current helper remain distinct. Original policy landing and cleanup follow-up are separate phases."
